[11:34] I built the agent and saved it, but it has not been tested on any calls. `public-test-set.json` is empty for this brief, so there were no practice customers and I did not run `tools/run_cases.py`. The only checks are the workflow checker, a local run of the date and amount code, and my reading of the graph against all 47 rules.
[11:34] 
[11:34] **Memos.** OM-3 (3 February 2026) is dated before the 2 March 2026 policy extract, so the extract replaces it. Its 20:00 callback limit and its 10-business-day car-loan rule are not used. OM-17 (9 October 2026) does apply:
[11:34] - Callbacks are booked only from 09:00 to 17:00, today or the next business day, and later than `now`.
[11:34] - Customers 8 to 45 days late get the 6th business day as their deadline.
[11:34] 
[11:34] **How the agent works**
[11:34] - **Dates and amounts are computed in code, not by the model.** Two code steps work out today, the deadline for the customer's band, the attempt-1 date, the callback window and the exact list of dates a promise may use. I checked them on four `now` values: a Wednesday, a Friday at 16:59, a Saturday, and the Friday before the 26 October holiday. The holiday is skipped correctly.
[11:34] - **Identity.** The two security questions use the bank's own `verified`, `hint` and `wrong_answers_left` answers to move on, ask again or close as `failed`.
[11:34] - **Persuasion attempts.** There is one step per attempt. The late band gets a second attempt and the early band does not, so an offer cannot be made more times than the brief allows.
[11:34] - **Closing.** Paid, dispute, hardship, restructuring, wrong number, deceased and "unclear after the second ask" each go to a fixed close. `close_call` runs on its own step, and only the hang-up comes after it. The goodbye and the confirmation-text sentence are fixed lines.
[11:34] - **Honesty.** "Recorded" is only said after `create_promise` succeeds. A second failure closes as `no_promise` / `service_error` and tells the customer.
[11:34] 
[11:34] **Three choices the brief leaves open**
[11:34] - **Weekend callbacks.** I read "today or the next business day" literally, so a call on a Saturday offers Saturday 09:00 to 17:00 as well as Monday.
[11:34] - **Failed transfer.** The brief does not say what to do. The agent says it could not connect them and closes as `no_promise` / `service_error`.
[11:34] - **Refusing to give a callback time.** The brief does not cover a third party who won't say when the customer can be reached. The agent closes as `not_reached` / `no_callback`.
[11:34] 
